## Findings
1. blocking — brief:91 [severity: S1] [design: changes] `rebindPr` writes N to the queue binding before `reviewNotice`; a transient title, CODEOWNERS-screen, notice, or `gh pr edit` failure makes the real `next` caller hold once, but its next run sees binding=N and advances to merge without retrying the required review, while W-462-b3 covers success only. Replace brief:91 with: “`rebindPr` runs `fetchTrunk`, `repoSlug` and `reviewNotice` first; only `notice.ok` may write binding N; any earlier failure leaves the old binding unchanged so `next` remains at rebind, and a binding-write failure holds before merge.” [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: packages/cli/src/next-queue.test.ts W-462-b3 reviewNotice failure cases
2. blocking — brief:90 [severity: S1] [design: changes] `boundHead` errors are sent to `merge`, while differing or malformed bytes derive `rebind` without reading merge mode: an unreadable queue-mode binding can bypass re-review, and removing the queue while a stale unequal binding exists makes a direct-mode caller perform rebind writes instead of the existing direct-mode hold; existing rows cover only unreadable direct mode and an equal valid binding. Replace brief:90 with: “The derivation first reads merge mode: direct mode leaves binding interpretation to existing `mergeGate` (absent proceeds; present or error holds); merge-queue mode accepts an absent binding or exactly one well-formed OID, derives rebind only for a differing OID, and `deriveNext` holds on unreadable, malformed, symlinked or over-bound content.” [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: packages/cli/src/next-queue.test.ts W-462-b3 plus W-199-b2
3. blocking — brief:65 [severity: S1] [design: changes] A plausible build or recorded-red command can leave a tracked or untracked path; because `checkSeries` reuses that worktree and ignores the final checkout result, later replays can observe contaminated state and `next --perform` can print the Patron command while the worktree is dirty or detached, which W-462-b2 does not test. Replace brief:65 with: “Promise restored: each build and replay is isolated, or its filesystem delta is rejected and cleaned; `performRewrite` emits no `patron:` line unless checkout back to `opus/<id>` at N succeeds and the original clean state is confirmed, and an uncleanable or unrestorable checkout holds with that limit stated.” [class: mechanism×replay-environment-not-pristine] — check: packages/cli/src/next-queue.test.ts W-462-b2 tracked-write, untracked-write and restore-failure cases

## Verdict
The signed brief has three design-changing S1 fail-closed gaps in rebind retry, binding interpretation, and in-place replay restoration.
